## P1 — DV and Assertion Priorities

The common assertion library for this batch should include:

* `VALID && !READY |=> VALID`.
* `VALID && !READY |=> $stable(payload)`.
* Accepted AW creates a write-address queue entry.
* Accepted W beats associate with the oldest applicable AXI4 AW stream.
* WLAST occurs exactly on beat `AWLEN+1`.
* BVALID is legal only after accepted AW and final accepted W.
* Every BID maps to one outstanding AWID.
* Accepted AR creates a read-request queue entry.
* RVALID/RID map to an outstanding AR.
* RLAST occurs exactly on beat `ARLEN+1`.
* Same-ID response ordering is preserved.
* Exactly one B response retires each write.
* Exactly `ARLEN+1` R beats retire each read.

The common constrained-random strategy should independently randomize:

* AWVALID initiation delay.
* AWREADY backpressure.
* WVALID beat gaps.
* WREADY backpressure.
* BVALID response latency.
* BREADY backpressure.
* ARVALID initiation delay.
* ARREADY backpressure.
* RVALID initial latency and inter-beat gaps.
* RREADY backpressure.

